{
  "__SECTION_ROOT_README__": "",
  "Disfigure Mod Manager": "",
  "A simple desktop manager for Disfigure BepInEx plugins. It detects the game folder, installs BepInEx when needed, and lets players install, update, enable, disable, and uninstall plugins from a public catalog without a GitHub account or token.": "",
  "Download": "",
  "Download Disfigure Mod Manager for Windows": "",
  "Extract the ZIP and run DisfigureModManager.exe. The manager automatically looks for Disfigure in Steam libraries; use Browse if the game is elsewhere.": "",
  "Linux and Steam Deck players running Disfigure through Proton should select a Windows x64 IL2CPP BepInEx package in the manager. A native Linux BepInEx package is not compatible with the Windows game under Proton.": "",
  "The manager prevents plugin changes while Disfigure is running. If the game is open when a change is requested, close it first; the restart reminder only appears when the game is actually running.": "",
  "Available plugins": "",
  "Disfigure Translation Mod: Adds community language translations and supports Disfigure 1.0.": "",
  "Sandbox Mode: Opens an in-run panel for upgrades, timer controls, and enemy spawning.": "",
  "The manager reads plugins.json, so new plugins and releases can be added without publishing a new manager build.": "",
  "How to use it": "",
  "Open the manager and confirm the detected Disfigure folder.": "",
  "Install a compatible BepInEx version if prompted.": "",
  "Use Available Plugins to install plugins from the catalog.": "",
  "Use Installed Plugins to update, enable, disable, or uninstall them.": "",
  "Translation Mod controls": "",
  "Open the language menu": "",
  "Reload translations": "",
  "Force a text rescan": "",
  "Supported languages are English, Spanish, French, Russian, German, Brazilian Portuguese, Simplified Chinese, Japanese, and Polish.": "",
  "Translations are machine-assisted and may contain mistakes.": "",
  "Help translate": "",
  "Current translations and blank community worksheets are available in the community-translations folder, organized by full language name.": "",
  "Anyone can fork the repository, edit a language file in GitHub, and submit a pull request for review.": "",
  "See Contributing translations for instructions.": "",
  "Sandbox Mode": "",
  "While in a run, press F5 to open the sandbox menu. Select any upgrades, perks, or mutations you want, with no limit.": "",
  "You can change the time to whatever you want. This is useful for fighting bosses or testing a late-game build.": "",
  "You can spawn any enemy. A late-game miniboss spawned very early will be extremely slow, which is useful for testing damage without worrying about dying.": "",
  "You cannot gain score while Sandbox Mode is enabled. Disable it in the mod manager to play a normal run.": "",
